body:
This function can also be simplified a bit, the `match` is not necessary here.
```rust
fn get_dart_version() -> Option<String> {
    let output = Command::new("dart").arg("--version").output().ok()?;
    if !output.status.success() {
        log::warn!(
            "Non-Zero exit code '{}' when executing `dart --version`",
            output.status
        );
        return None;
    }

    String::from_utf8(output.stderr).ok()
}
``` 
Another notable change is propagating None instead of panicing when the utf-8 decode fails, so that starship won't break if dart is really screwed up.

